---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import TrainingWorkspace from '../components/TrainingWorkspace';
import '../styles/global.css';
---
<Base title="Dead Hang Training - Workouts, Timer & Protocol" description="Free dead hang timer, training log and practical guides. Compare your hold, plan a manageable session and find equipment that fits your space.">
  <Nav />
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="home-hero shell">
      <div class="hero-copy"><p class="dh-eyebrow">One bar. A practice you can measure.</p><h1>HANG.<br/><span>TRAIN.</span><br/>REPEAT.</h1><p class="hero-intro">A timer for your next set. A log for the holds you actually do. Clear guides for the questions in between.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="dh-btn" href="#timer">Start a session</a><a class="text-link" href="/dead-hang-calculator/">Compare my hold →</a></div><p class="small-copy">Free tools. No account. Training history stays on your device.</p></div>
      <figure class="hero-figure"><svg class="hang-illustration" viewBox="0 0 520 500" role="img" aria-label="Illustration of a person hanging from a horizontal bar"><defs><pattern id="training-grid" width="40" height="40" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M40 0H0V40" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity=".1"/></pattern></defs><rect width="520" height="500" fill="var(--color-surface)"/><rect x="20" y="20" width="480" height="460" fill="url(#training-grid)"/><path d="M60 66H460" stroke="var(--color-primary)" stroke-width="12"/><path d="M80 46V86M440 46V86" stroke="var(--color-primary)" stroke-width="4"/><path d="M170 72L203 157L239 188M350 72L317 157L281 188" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-text)" stroke-width="18" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="260" cy="153" r="23" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-text)" stroke-width="9"/><path d="M235 188Q260 180 285 188L282 296H238Z" fill="var(--color-primary)"/><path d="M250 297L230 365L229 425M270 297L291 365L291 425" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-text)" stroke-width="18" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M214 427H236M284 427H309" stroke="var(--color-text)" stroke-width="10" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M52 456H468" stroke="var(--color-border)" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M375 155H435M375 296H435M415 155V296" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-text-faint)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 6"/></svg><figcaption><span class="dh-mono">THE PRACTICE</span> Grip. Hang. Step down. Record.</figcaption><div class="hero-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div><p>Start from your own baseline.<br/>Build a record worth comparing.</p></figure>
    </section>
    <section class="route-strip shell" aria-label="Choose your next step">
      <a href="/dead-hang-time-by-age/"><span>UNDERSTAND YOUR TIME</span><strong>What does my hold mean?</strong><span class="route-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a href="/training-programs/"><span>BUILD A ROUTINE</span><strong>Find a starting plan</strong><span class="route-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a href="/equipment-guide/"><span>SET UP YOUR SPACE</span><strong>Choose a suitable bar</strong><span class="route-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </section>
    <section id="timer" class="workspace-section shell"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="dh-eyebrow">Your training bench</p><h2>Make the next hold count.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/training-log/">Open dedicated timer & log →</a></div><TrainingWorkspace client:load /><noscript><p>The timer and log need JavaScript. Use the <a href="/training-programs/#print-plan">printable session planner</a> with a stopwatch.</p></noscript></section>
    <section id="protocol" class="editorial-section shell"><div><p class="dh-eyebrow">First session?</p><h2>Start with control.<br/>Keep the record simple.</h2></div><div><p>Use a securely fitted bar and a stable way to step down. Choose a hold you can end under control. Keep your feet supported if you need assistance. Stop if the movement causes pain.</p><p>Record the same kind of hold each time. An assisted hang and an unassisted hang should have separate baselines.</p><a class="text-link" href="/how-to-deadhang/">Read the form guide →</a></div></section>
    <section id="science" class="evidence-section shell"><p class="dh-eyebrow">What the evidence says</p><h2>Grip strength matters.<br/>A stopwatch is not a health score.</h2><p>Published grip-strength research often measures squeezing force with a dynamometer. Those findings do not give us population percentiles for timed dead hangs or a way to predict an individual's lifespan. Our calculator compares your own numbers.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="text-link" href="https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0113637">Read the grip-strength study</a><a class="text-link" href="/editorial-standards/">Our editorial standards</a></div></section>
    <section class="reading-list shell"><p class="dh-eyebrow">Keep learning</p><h2>Useful answers, next.</h2>{[
      ['Dead hang times by age', 'Understand the limits of age comparisons.', '/dead-hang-time-by-age/'],
      ['Dead hang workout guide', 'Form, routine and progression in one place.', '/deadhang-guide/'],
      ['Equipment for home training', 'Mounting options, space and buying checks.', '/equipment-guide/'],
      ['The dead hang world record', 'A different kind of endurance.', '/dead-hang-world-record/'],
    ].map(([title, copy, href]) => <a href={href}><strong>{title}</strong><span>{copy}</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>)}</section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
